# .agentremember — Localism project memory
# Agent MUST re-read this file at the start of every session and re-read any listed
# file before editing it. Do not rely on session memory.

## Non-negotiable workflow
- FINISH ALL FILE EDITS FIRST, THEN BUILD ONCE. Never run `npm run build` after
  editing a single file. Batch edits, then one build + one lint at the end.
- Do NOT kill running `next-server` processes. They may belong to other 9router
  sessions. Start new servers on a NEW port instead (e.g. `next start -p 401x`).
- If `next dev`/`next build` fails, run `npx next build --webpack` to get the real
  error (Turbopack often hides it behind "Error evaluating Node.js code").

## Architectural rules (source of truth: RULES.md / .agentrules)
1. ZERO SERVER CALLS — all computation 100% in-browser. Never suggest external API.
2. THREAD SAFETY — heavy work (WASM, PDF, image transforms) MUST go to Web Workers.
3. MEMORY HYGIENE — `URL.revokeObjectURL` on every object URL; terminate workers;
   no RAM leaks.
4. STACK — Next.js App Router, Tailwind CSS, Lucide React, Shadcn UI components.
5. NO HALLUCINATED LIBRARIES — pure Web APIs (Canvas, FileReader, Crypto) or
   battle-tested libs (pdf-lib, @ffmpeg/ffmpeg v0.12+).

## Design system (Hallmark · genre: modern-minimal · theme: Cobalt dark/zinc · macrostructure: Workbench)
- Fonts: Geist + Geist Mono via next/font (layout.tsx). Preserve them.
- Palette: full dark mode. tokens.css `@theme` — paper=zinc-950 (oklch 13%), panel=zinc-900/50,
  rule=zinc-800/700, one electric cobalt accent oklch(74% 0.14 256) lightened for dark, ok/error status.
  NO graphite tokens anymore (replaced by panel). Read tokens.css before styling.
- Colors MUST reference tokens (bg-paper, bg-panel, text-ink, border-rule-2, text-accent…).
  Never inline hex/oklch/rgb in components. Add new values to tokens.css `@theme` first.
- tokens.css lives at project ROOT; globals.css imports it as `@import "../../tokens.css";`
  (relative to src/app — do NOT "fix" this to a single `..`; that path is wrong).
- No italic headers. No invented metrics. No `transition-all` / `transition: all`.
- Focus: `:focus-visible` global outline, instant (never animated).
- Motion: `--ease-out` etc from tokens. Reduced-motion block in globals.css must stay
  (kills .reveal + .status-dot pulse).
- `overflow-x: clip` on html AND body (globals.css) — never `hidden`.
- Tab strip uses `no-scrollbar` utility (defined in globals.css via @utility) for horizontal scroll.

